# M2-ETERNAL-ORIGINAL-UNPROVED, ETERNAL-QUALIFICATION-RETAINED-REFERENCE (steps/defects.md): an eternal (qualified)
# original starts the M2 closure with its constructed body, so `call: E` is certified; the branch's retained send
# qualifies, its primitive owned by the arena and its signature contained by its parent. E writes no local data
# field, so the unary call needs no var (the author, LMX_blog/2026-10-15.md). Entry 7.
independent:
    const:
        immutable:
            (): E
                sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 7; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
            end: E
        end: immutable
    end: const
end: independent
call: E
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 90; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
